a8773635d35","position":{"commit_sha":"0aa309f4cb15dec4d47bb7ac6f8de342e8b20d6b","position":"1786169910088648001-39414ea2-a587-4c4e-bddb-ea8773635d35"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"be97cff39a7774d8622ec056f196fce44249963ee675c3b1229b5ab242bcb40d","event_uuid":"ddd0ace2-0f09-4aef-a00c-80fc13c263cd","position":{"commit_sha":"0aa309f4cb15dec4d47bb7ac6f8de342e8b20d6b","position":"1786169910660900001-ddd0ace2-0f09-4aef-a00c-80fc13c263cd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786047085164806001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"Scope: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/**` (95 files, 27,284 LOC, 42% comment density). ~970 lines leave — the largest shard.\n\nDominant category: 28 sites carrying 'RELOCATED VERBATIM ... forced by the LOCKED 800-line cap' (~75 lines), already single-sourced in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`, AGENTS.md and ADR 0058.\n\nFour new ADRs proposed, each consolidating an argument restated 4-8 times: field-convergence fit-then-normalize (8 sites); pagination-stall aborts past fail-open handlers (3 independent arguments, 3 prior incidents); unmapped relations skipped not approximated; core owns the value maps. Plus amendments to ADR 0028, 0055 §(g), 0031, 0035.\n\nVerified stale: `_backend_registry.py:3` 'STUB: signatures pinned, bodies to be implemented' while `select_backend` is imported by 13 modules; the S3/S4-not-landed notes in `_backend.py` and `adapters/jira/backend.py`.\n\nHeadroom: `_ref_lock.py` 1 -> ~21, `dispatch_one.py` 14 -> ~57, `inbound_differ.py` 18 -> ~66, `binding_store.py` 18 -> ~33, `fetcher.py` 29 -> ~80.\n\nThis subtree's comments are overwhelmingly measured external-API facts that cannot be re-derived from code. The do_not_move list is the most valuable output of the shard.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost; measured-fact and anti-refactor warnings stay verbatim\n\n## CORRECTION (plan-review BLOCK, criteria E4/G1G2/G6)\n\n### 1. The dominant-category count was wrong — re-measured\n\nThe body claims \"28 sites carrying 'RELOCATED VERBATIM ... forced by the LOCKED 800-line cap'\n(~75 lines)\". That is not borne out by the tree. Measured over\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/`:\n\n    $ grep -rn \"RELOCATED VERBATIM\" src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler | wc -l\n    6                       # 6 sites, ALL under adapters/jira_datacenter/\n    $ grep -rniE \"800-line|LOCKED 800|module-size cap\" src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler | wc -l\n    6                       # a SEPARATE, smaller set (transport.py, retry.py, transitions.py)\n    $ grep -rliE \"RELOCATED VERBATIM|800-line|LOCKED 800|module-size cap\" ... | wc -l\n    10                      # 10 distinct files carry EITHER marker\n\nNo single site carries the quoted combined marker. The two families are disjoint, and neither is\nclose to 28. The real figure is **~12 occurrences across 10 files**, not 28.\n\n**Consequence for the shard's headline yield.** The \"~970 lines leave\" estimate was built on the\ninflated count for its largest single category. That estimate is therefore UNRELIABLE and must not\nbe treated as a target. The implementer MEASURES the actual recoverable total and records it on\nthis ticket; the number is an output of the work, not an input to it. Do not manufacture\nrelocations to reach ~970.\n\n### 2. Write-ordering must cover the ADRs, not just `do_not_move`\n\nThe plan requires the `do_not_move` list to be appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit\nlands, but says nothing about ordering for the four proposed new ADRs (field-convergence\nfit-then-normalize; pagination-stall aborts past fail-open handlers; unmapped relations skipped not\napproximated; core owns the value maps) or the amendments to ADR 0028/0055/0031/0035.\n\nThose ADRs are the single-source DESTINATIONS for the arguments currently restated 4-8 times. If a\ncomment citing \"see ADR NNNN\" is collapsed before ADR NNNN exists, the citation dangles and the\nargument is simply LOST — which is the opposite of relocation and is not recoverable from the diff\nby a later reader.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (supersedes the list above)\n\n- [ ] The shard's `do_not_move` list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Each new ADR and each amendment EXISTS AND IS COMMITTED before any comment that will cite it\n      is collapsed or deleted — destination first, then the relocation\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination; nothing is deleted\n      without a destination that already exists\n- [ ] The ACTUAL recoverable line count is measured and recorded on this ticket, replacing the\n      unreliable ~970 estimate. The measured marker counts (6 RELOCATED VERBATIM, 6 cap mentions,\n      10 files) are the corrected baseline\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are CORRECTED where they document a live invariant, deleted only\n      where obsolete — specifically `_backend_registry.py`'s \"STUB: signatures pinned, bodies to be\n      implemented\" (false: `select_backend` is imported by 13 modules) and the S3/S4-not-landed\n      notes in `_backend.py` and `adapters/jira/backend.py`\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost; measured external-API facts and anti-refactor warnings\n      stay VERBATIM (this subtree's comments are overwhelmingly measured facts that cannot be\n      re-derived from code — the do_not_move list is the most valuable output of the shard)\n- [ ] No behaviour change: the reconciler's tests pass unchanged\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","managed_refs":[["parent","373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","parent_status_uuid":"39414ea2-a587-4c4e-bddb-ea8773635d35","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"9ce8-8ff1-0832-4825","ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: reconciler subtree","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["02254c99-cd1e-44aa-8b06-badaaab608ed","5af5bae2-c3e0-4370-a2fc-91e8361c1baa","7d83f433-988d-48e0-8bd9-cf2bf338ca7f","0f7945c1-fa99-4434-8dd0-6a6858167aba","39414ea2-a587-4c4e-bddb-ea8773635d35","ddd0ace2-0f09-4aef-a00c-80fc13c263cd"]},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786169910660900002,"uuid":"eaccf040-e18a-4a08-a951-73a1285079d7"}